description:
Found while building fz-sc8.72. `%{m | :a => 3}` does not parse: "expected keyword entry". Elixir accepts any key expression with => in a map update, and keyword syntax (a: 3) is sugar for atom keys. The update parser (src/parser) accepts only the keyword form; map literals already accept both. Fold the two so the update reads the same entry grammar as the literal. Oracle fixture with an atom key via =>, a string key, and a mixed update. Deviation from Elixir; not needed by the distiller.

Also found while building fz-3sy.12: an update does not parse with a newline on either side of the bar. A newline before it (`%{
  b
  | x: 1
}`, the layout mix format gives a long update) fails with "expected `=>`, got Newline"; a newline after it (`%{b |
  x: 1
}`) fails with "expected keyword entry, got Newline". Newlines after each comma are accepted. The same fold fixes it: the entries after the bar are the literal's entries. Add both layouts to the oracle fixture.
